// omarchy-kids-trimmed.jsonc — the omarchy-menu user extension for a kid whose
// profile says `menu=trimmed` (SPEC.md R-DESK-4).
//
// VERIFIED MECHANISM (try-omarchy VM, Omarchy 4.0.2, 2026-09-21). omarchy-menu
// is a Quickshell plugin; it reads the stock entries from
// /usr/share/omarchy/default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc and merges the user
// extension at $HOME/.config/omarchy/extensions/omarchy-menu.jsonc
// (shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml, `userMenuPath`). MenuModel.mergeMenuSources()
// merges the two **by id**, field by field, the user file winning. An entry is
// hidden when its `when:` shell expression evaluates false
// (Menu.qml `evaluateGuards`). So a hide is the same id with `when: "false"` —
// not a "hide" list, which this file used to guess at.
//
// Where it is applied: provisioning copies this file into the kid's own
// ~/.config/omarchy/extensions/omarchy-menu.jsonc when the profile's
// `menu = trimmed` (default for bands 3-5, 6-8 and 9-12). It is the kid's own
// file, so it is presentation, not a lock: a kid who edits it can see the rows
// again, and every action behind them still fails their account's permissions
// (polkit/sudo deny). The enforcement is the account, never this file (I-3).
//
// Levels 1 and 2 never reach this menu at all: Level 1 runs no shell, and
// Level 2 runs the Kids launcher with Super+Space rebound to its own picker
// (Appendix E). This file is what makes Level 3's stock desktop honest for a
// kid, alongside the kid's trimmed shell.json (no omarchy.system-update
// widget, which is where "Pending Omarchy Migrations" comes from).
{
  "install": {"when": "false"},
  "remove": {"when": "false"},
  "update": {"when": "false"},
  "setup": {"when": "false"}
}
